# Observability Lab: Datadog APM & Service Map Flow Investigation

## 1\. Investigation Summary & Topology Context

The Datadog investigation identified a production performance degradation centered on payment\-api. The service showed a **14.2% error rate** and **4850 ms P95 latency**.

The overall transaction flow was:

web\-storefront → checkout\-service → payment\-api → postgres\-payment\-db

The payment\-api also communicated with the external stripe\-external\-gateway.

Analysis of the Datadog Service Map and APM trace showed that the main bottleneck was PostgreSQL database lock contention. A SELECT ... FOR UPDATE query waited approximately 5 seconds and timed out. This caused HTTP 500 failures in payment\-api, which propagated upstream to checkout\-service and affected the web\-storefront.

