## Root Cause Summary

The root cause of the production degradation was **PostgreSQL row\-lock contention combined with very high database connection utilization**.

The query:

SELECT \* FROM payment\_accounts WHERE account\_id = ? FOR UPDATE

spent **5008 ms** waiting and eventually failed with a PostgreSQL statement timeout. At the same time, the database had **98/100 active connections** and **34 operations in the lock wait queue**.

The resulting database failures propagated through:

postgres\-payment\-db → payment\-api → checkout\-service → web\-storefront

The external Stripe gateway remained healthy and was not the source of the outage.

